                  <provenance type="#i"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_94">Cambridge,
                        Cambridgeshire. Franciscan convent. </orgName><p>'Fratris Ric' bryngkelei |
                        Ex dono venerabilis generose Katerine Wyndyssor | .x. s.' (in a fine hand on
                        sig. [aj]).</p><p>Richard Brynkley OFM was a member of the Cambridge convent
                        in 1489, still in 1493, in 1505--6, and later. He was elected prior
                        provincial of the order in England in 1518, vacated in 1526 (Emden, BRUC,
                        103). He was learned in Greek and Hebrew and his name as owner or borrower
                        occurs in eight other books, listed by Emden.</p></provenance>
